33
00:01:32.977 --> 00:01:37.560
"We Got The Beat" was released 40 years ago.

34
00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:41.060
Give me a memory from 40 years ago if you don't mind.

35
00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:43.160
Mine is when we recorded it.

36
00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:45.190
And we went in the recording studio,

37
00:01:45.190 --> 00:01:48.560 line:15%
and ready and rearing to get "We Got The Beat",

38
00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:51.060 line:15%
and we played it and then we played it again.

39
00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:52.230 line:15%
Then we played it again.

40
00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:53.290
Then we played it again.

41
00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:57.727
And after the tenth try our producer Richard said,

42
00:01:57.727 --> 00:01:59.350
"Okay, let's take a break."

43
00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:00.763
And he ordered pizza.

44
00:02:03.110 --> 00:02:05.010
It was either the magic sauce in the pizza,

45
00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:08.286
or the stars aligned while we were eating.

46
00:02:08.286 --> 00:02:11.120
Or maybe both, but that the 11th take was magic.

47
00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:14.270
And we are just so happy that

48
00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:15.980
we get to share that with you today.

49
00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:19.293
I love being behind the scenes, that's so exciting.

50
00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:24.680
What was the inspiration for that album cover?

51
00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:27.600
The cover as well as what was inside and all you guys

52
00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:29.600
was just such a life changer.

53
00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:34.140
It's a really iconic image and I don't know...

54
00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:36.450 line:15%
You realize that our main goal was not to

55
00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:40.360 line:15%
date the record and not like see it 20 years later.

56
00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:42.630 line:15%
And oh, look at those hairstyles and whatnot.

57
00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:45.520
I believe it was Belinda's idea, was it babe?

58
00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:46.451
Was it your idea?

59
00:02:46.451 --> 00:02:48.210
Yeah.

60
00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:50.269
Yeah, I don't know how it came about.

61
00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:53.350 line:15%
I thought that...

62
00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:56.080 line:15%
Being in towels and masks,

63
00:02:56.080 --> 00:03:01.080 line:15%
and about beauty, and not being any sort of dated fashion,

64
00:03:01.792 --> 00:03:04.020 line:15%
it's a timeless cover.

65
00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:06.400
I know speaking for myself and the band

66
00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:07.670
that we're so happy to be able to

67
00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:09.383
celebrate this birthday with you.

68
00:03:11.235 --> 00:03:13.070
We feel like you're really one of us,

69
00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:14.696
to be perfectly honest.

70
00:03:14.696 --> 00:03:17.696
(audience clapping)

71
00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:21.320
I know I wouldn't be the same person

72
00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:24.900
